    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n62509" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λεπτόλογ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>speaking subtly,
			quibbling</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρένες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					876
				</span></i>
			 (hex.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VS</u>
				1.21.1
			</span></i>: in good sense, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλ᾽ ὅ γε λεπτολόγος σκῆπτρον Ἄρατος
					ἔχει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ptol.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ach.Tat.
				<u>Intr. Arat.</u>
				p.79
			</span></i> M.</div>
